---
import PublicPage from '../../components/public/PublicPage.astro';
---

<PublicPage
  label="Legal"
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Tosder Communities collects, why we collect it, and the choices you have."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 17, 2026</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account details from Neon Auth: email address, display name, and session data.</li>
      <li>Your creator profile: username, bio, avatar, and optional social links.</li>
      <li>Content you create: templates, trips, days, items, checklist entries, reviews, saves, and likes.</li>
      <li>Usage records needed to calculate qualified uses, moderate content, pay rewards, and keep an audit trail.</li>
      <li>An opaque visitor cookie used to deduplicate template views. Only a hash is stored with the view event; raw IP addresses are not stored for views.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide sign-in, planning tools, creator publishing, and public discovery.</li>
      <li>Calculate qualified uses and competition rankings from the usage ledger.</li>
      <li>Moderate reports, protect members, and prevent abuse.</li>
      <li>Produce aggregate creator analytics without exposing traveler identities.</li>
      <li>Meet legal, tax, and payout obligations for rewards.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we share</h2>
    <p>
      We use infrastructure providers for hosting, database, authentication, and email delivery. We do
      not sell personal data. Public pages show creator profiles, templates, aggregate counts, and
      reviews; they never show private trips or traveler contact details.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account and planning data is kept while your account is active.</li>
      <li>Usage and audit events are kept for competition integrity and dispute resolution; privileged audit events are retained for up to 7 years.</li>
      <li>Deleted trips remove their itinerary and source attribution. Audit records may remain for integrity.</li>
      <li>Backups are retained for a limited operational window.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      Essential cookies keep you signed in and deduplicate views. Theme preference is stored in local
      storage. We do not use advertising cookies or third-party ad trackers.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can edit your profile and content, delete trips, archive templates, and request account
      deletion or an export. Contact us to exercise access, correction, or deletion rights. Some records
      may be retained where required for legal, fraud-prevention, or payout reconciliation purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The service is intended for adults. Do not create an account if you are under 18.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@tosder.com">privacy@tosder.com</a>. Replace this address
      with the monitored launch address before public launch.
    </p>

    <p class="note">
      This policy is an operational draft. Legal counsel must review it before public launch.
    </p>
  </article>
</PublicPage>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 68ch; }
  .updated, .note { color: var(--color-text-subtle); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
  .note { margin-top: var(--space-5); padding-top: var(--space-3); border-top: var(--border-width) solid var(--color-border); }
  h2 { margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-2); font-size: var(--text-lg); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold); }
  p, li { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); }
  ul { margin: 0; padding-left: var(--space-5); }
  li { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
  a { color: var(--color-text); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
